From 699b607f3b0903353e6914976c6a205d26256f32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meteowrite <dtodorovtu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:36:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/sun4i: Allow interrupts to be used as wakeup sources

The A10/A13 interrupt controller has no wake configuration of its own,
and these SoCs only support suspend-to-idle, where the controller keeps
running: any interrupt left enabled wakes the system.

Without an irq_set_wake() callback, enable_irq_wake() fails with -ENXIO
for interrupts routed through this controller (e.g. the NMI line used by
the AXP209 PMIC and RTCs), so drivers that arm wakeup in their suspend
path either warn or abort the suspend.

Set IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE so that wakeup sources can be armed.

Tested on a PocketBook 624 (A13): s2idle wakeup through a PCF8563
alarm (NMI line, shared with the AXP209) and gpio-keys/LRADC keys.

Signed-off-by: meteowrite <dtodorovtu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c
index b095d45da75d..8e564e5b6dfc 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c
@@ -87,7 +87,8 @@ static struct irq_chip sun4i_irq_chip = {
 	.irq_eoi	= sun4i_irq_ack,
 	.irq_mask	= sun4i_irq_mask,
 	.irq_unmask	= sun4i_irq_unmask,
-	.flags		= IRQCHIP_EOI_THREADED | IRQCHIP_EOI_IF_HANDLED,
+	.flags		= IRQCHIP_EOI_THREADED | IRQCHIP_EOI_IF_HANDLED |
+			  IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE,
 };
 
 static int sun4i_irq_map(struct irq_domain *d, unsigned int virq,
-- 
